{% comment %}
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║  PHOTO ROLODEX — Host Page block                                 ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Paste this into a "Lava Application Content Block" (not a       ║
║  plain HTML Content block -- this specific block type is what    ║
║  auto-registers HTMX and knows how to resolve the "^/" endpoint  ║
║  shorthand used below and in the two endpoint files). Set the    ║
║  block's "Application" setting to the "rolodex" LavaApplication. ║
║  This is the ONLY piece of the game that lives on a page rather  ║
║  than inside a LavaEndpoint -- it draws the outer shell and      ║
║  renders the "setup" endpoint's content directly into it.        ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Requires the "rolodex" LavaApplication with its "setup" and     ║
║  "game" GET LavaEndpoints already created (see the two           ║
║  companion .lava files and DEPLOYMENT.md).                       ║
║                                                                  ║
║  REQUIREMENTS                                                    ║
║  • Rock RMS 18.0 or later. This is the version that added both    ║
║    the LavaApplication/LavaEndpoint feature and the built-in      ║
║    {[ dropdown ]} Lava shortcode the setup screen's List field     ║
║    uses -- confirm Admin Tools > CMS includes "Lava               ║
║    Applications" before building this out.                        ║
║  • SQL Lava commands enabled on BOTH LavaEndpoints (set           ║
║    "Enabled Lava Commands" to include "sql" on each one --        ║
║    this is per-endpoint, separate from the System Settings        ║
║    toggle blocks use). Neither endpoint needs anything beyond      ║
║    "sql" -- sources are Person Tags, looked up with plain SQL     ║
║    joins against Tag/TaggedItem, so no entity command is used.     ║
║  • This block below uses {% renderlavaendpoint %} to render the   ║
║    "setup" endpoint's content directly during this page's own     ║
║    render, instead of an hx-get/hx-trigger="load" round trip.     ║
║    That command has been available since 18.0; 18.2 added a fix  ║
║    for parsing a querystring inside the route parameter, which    ║
║    doesn't affect this build since the initial route has none.    ║
║    Confirmed: unlike LavaEndpoints, this Content Block does not   ║
║    need "renderlavaendpoint" separately enabled anywhere.         ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
{% endcomment %}

<style>
/*
  Per the Rock UI skill (triumph-techkit:rock-ui), components/utilities/CSS
  variables come first and custom CSS is a last resort. What's left here is
  only markup Rock's own components can't produce without pulling in Rock's
  client-side JS, which would break the "no JavaScript" requirement for this
  game:
    - .rd-mode-group: a JS-free segmented radio control. Rock's documented
      radio-button-list and toggle controls both depend on Rock's own
      scripts (js-rockradiobuttonlist / js-toggle-*) to manage the active
      state, so they're not an option here. This uses the native
      :checked + label sibling selector instead.
    - .rd-flip-details: the tap-to-reveal card, built on native
      <details>/<summary> so the reveal needs no script at all.
    - .rd-choices-grid .btn: Bootstrap's .btn sets white-space: nowrap by
      default, which would clip a long person's name instead of wrapping it.
    - .rd-photo-card: a plain aspect-ratio property instead of Rock's
      ratio-square utility, which relies on a padding-bottom technique that
      expects an absolutely-positioned child -- not worth the risk on the
      single most important element on the screen.
    - .rd-more-info: the optional "more about this person" panel, also
      built on native <details>/<summary> for the same JS-free reason as
      the flip card. Unlike the flip card, its summary stays visible when
      open (native toggle behavior) so it can be collapsed again.

  Any value below that isn't a structural/behavioral necessity (radius,
  color) references a Rock CSS variable rather than a hardcoded hex or px.
*/
#rolodex-app {
  max-width: 480px;
}

.rd-mode-group {
  display: flex;
  width: 100%;
}
.rd-mode-group input[type="radio"] {
  position: absolute;
  opacity: 0;
  width: 0;
  height: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.rd-mode-group label {
  flex: 1;
  text-align: center;
  margin: 0;
  cursor: pointer;
  border-radius: 0;
}
.rd-mode-group label:first-of-type { border-radius: var(--rounded-xsmall) 0 0 var(--rounded-xsmall); }
.rd-mode-group label:last-of-type  { border-radius: 0 var(--rounded-xsmall) var(--rounded-xsmall) 0; }
.rd-mode-group input[type="radio"]:checked + label {
  background-color: var(--color-primary);
  color: #fff;
  border-color: var(--color-primary);
  z-index: 1;
}

.rd-flip-details > summary {
  list-style: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  text-align: center;
}
.rd-flip-details > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.rd-flip-details[open] > summary { display: none; }

.rd-choices-grid .btn {
  white-space: normal;
}

.rd-photo-card {
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
}

.rd-more-info > summary {
  list-style: none;
  cursor: pointer;
}
.rd-more-info > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.rd-more-info-body {
  font-size: 0.9rem;
}
</style>

{% comment %}
  {% renderlavaendpoint %} calls the "setup" LavaEndpoint server-side and
  drops its returned content right here, as part of this page's own
  render -- no spinner, no extra HTTP round trip for the first screen.
  ^/{applicationSlug}/{endpointSlug} is the same shorthand used for
  hx-get/hx-post elsewhere in this build; update "rolodex" here if you
  use a different LavaApplication slug. method:'get' matches the
  endpoint's HTTP Method setting (GET is also the command's default if
  omitted, but it's spelled out here for clarity). Confirmed:
  renderlavaendpoint needs no separate "Enabled Lava Commands" setting
  on this Content Block.

  Every link the setup/game endpoints render afterward still targets
  #rolodex-app via hx-get, so the rest of the game plays out with
  normal HTMX swaps -- only this very first screen skips the round
  trip.
{% endcomment %}
<div id="rolodex-app" class="mx-auto px-2">
  {% renderlavaendpoint route:'^/rolodex/setup' method:'get' %}
</div>
